        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0b42461a-b4dc-56ed-9296-13dbcc8cf9ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edmund White, Charles Silverstein, Jean Genet\n- Works: Terre Haute, The Joy of Gay Sex, A Boy's Own Story, The Beautiful Room Is Empty, The Farewell Symphony\n- Roles: novelist, memoirist, essayist, playwright, biographer\n\nFacts:\n- Edmund Valentine White III was born on January 13, 1940, and he is an American novelist, memoirist, and essayist on literary and social topics.\n- Edmund White co-wrote The Joy of Gay Sex with Charles Silverstein, and the book was published in 1977.\n- Edmund White published the autobiographical novel A Boy's Own Story in 1982.\n- Edmund White published the autobiographical novel The Beautiful Room Is Empty in 1988.\n- Edmund White published the autobiographical novel The Farewell Symphony in 1997.\n- Edmund White wrote a biography of Jean Genet.\n- Edmund White wrote the play Terre Haute, which was published in 2006.",
